(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["da-easy-2025-005"]={"v":1,"id":"da-easy-2025-005","title":"Basic Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","code":"DA","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI","seriesId":"da-easy-2025","num":5,"category":"basic","year":"2025","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI"},"source":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Data_Science_and_AI/009_Basic Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tIn a 500 meters race <em>B</em> starts 45 meter ahead of <em>A</em> when <em>A</em> wins the race <em>B</em> is still 35 meters behind.<br />\n\tWhat is the ratio of the speeds of <em>B</em> and <em>A</em> assuming that both start at the same time?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"21 : 25"},{"key":"B","html":"20 : 25"},{"key":"C","html":"3 : 5"},{"key":"D","html":"7 : 5"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/553797af4d41ac91a6e4.png\" /></p>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tA garrison of 2200 men is provisioned for 16 weeks at the rate of 45g per day per man. How many men must leave the garrison so that the same provisions may last 24 weeks at 33 gm per day per man?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"180 men"},{"key":"B","html":"200 men"},{"key":"C","html":"220 men"},{"key":"D","html":"235 men"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/447603b48d1dfa3c68d4.png\" /></p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tYear wise annual rate of interest offered by two finance companies are shown in the following line graph.</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/328fe31fa8a5dc82935f.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tIf the amount invested in <em>P</em> and <em>Q</em> in 2006 are in the ratio 8 : 9, then the amount received after one year as interest from <em>P</em> and <em>Q</em> would be in the ratio:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4 : 3"},{"key":"B","html":"3 : 4"},{"key":"C","html":"2 : 3"},{"key":"D","html":"3 : 2"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/880c497de9eaeb35b7fe.png\" /></p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tIn the given diagram, circle A represents teachers who can teach physics, circle B represents teachers who can teach chemistry and circle C represents those who can teach mathematics. Among the regions marked <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f308b824ea937a27c8d.png\" /> the one which represents teachers who can teach physics and mathematics but not chemistry is</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5facd450b5e605d16a83.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/937247ceeac0e91b70f5.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<em>u</em></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<em>s</em></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<em>t<br />\n\t</em></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8bb26504d44f0da8fa3c.png\" /></p>"},{"n":5,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf the letters of the word “FATHER” are rearrange and all possible six letter words are formed and then written out as in a dictionary then rank of the word “FATHER” is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[261,261],"answerText":"261 (261 - 261)","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t261 (261 - 261)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/adba59c6ef5af0ffb569.png\" /></p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tSix persons A, B, C, D, E and F are standing in a row. C and D are standing close to each other alongside E. B is standing beside A only. A is fourth from F. Who are standing on the extremes?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A and F"},{"key":"B","html":"B and D"},{"key":"C","html":"B and F"},{"key":"D","html":"None of the above"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\tAs per data given,<br />\n\tCDE will be together in some order i.e.<br />\n\tCDE or ECD or DCE or EDC<br />\n\tSince, A is fourth from F, the possible combinations are<br />\n\tF _ _ _ A_ or _F _ _ _ A<br />\n\tor<br />\n\tSince E, C and D are together and B is besides A, the possible combination is F(ECD)AB.<br />\n\tThus, B and F have to be at extremes.</p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>M</em><sub>1</sub> - <em>M</em><sub>2</sub> represents a mirror surface,</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/14e7cb9f47faaa44a989.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following sentence is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"I have five Ten rupee notes"},{"key":"B","html":"I have five Ten rupees notes"},{"key":"C","html":"I have five Ten rupee note"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\tThe singular noun &lsquo;rupee&rsquo; is used before note or notes. The word &#39;rupee&#39; should be used in the singular form and the word &#39;note&#39; should be used in the plural form.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\t______ you have a doubt, why not go and verify? I shall be waiting in the shade_____ this Banyan tree till you come back_____ me.<br />\n\tThe option that best fills the blanks in the above sentence would be:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"if; under; on"},{"key":"B","html":"as; of; for"},{"key":"C","html":"as; of; at"},{"key":"D","html":"if; of; to"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)<br />\n\tSince the first sentence is a question, if is more appropriate than as. Shade of this tree and back to me are the appropriate usages.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tA well, whose diameter is 14 m, has been dug 10 m deep and the earth dug out is used to form an embankment 3 m wide around it. The height of the embankment will be _____ m. [Upto one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9,10],"answerText":"9.6 (9.0 - 10.0)","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t9.6 (9.0 - 10.0)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/9432726fc3206c3596d8.png\" /></p>"},{"n":11,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tA coin is tossed 5 times. The probability of getting exactly 3 heads is ________. (Upto 2 decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.3,0.33],"answerText":"0.31 [0.30 - 0.33]","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.31 [0.30 - 0.33]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c3fd9c70836d73dc746b.png\" /></p>"},{"n":12,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following matrix:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c13b5d42803a07907d12.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tOut of all the eigen values, the minimum eigen value is _________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-6,-6],"answerText":"-6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t-6</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ffa5eeb7dac449685055.png\" /></p>"},{"n":13,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following Python code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9daa1de69f45c787a9d.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhat is the output of above code?</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[22,22],"answerText":"22","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t22</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91f1adc7dd154b1030f3.png\" /></p>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tAn container <em>P</em> contains 2 Red and 4 Green ball. Another container <em>Q</em> contains 5 Red and 7 Green balls. A ball is transferred from container to container <em>Q</em>, then a ball is drawn from container <em>Q</em>. The probability the ball is Red is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4b7ed2c2474ca5293774.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c029b7e2d4fec8eacb6.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c4/c422c64c9483d35b6a1f.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c0d9cf4902601b3ba0b.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e185b519870feb2bf353.png\" /></p>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab83accba8fd66a3f119.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1"},{"key":"B","html":"0"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<em>e</em></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"Undefined"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3d/3d9c6bcd381ae2979d4f.png\" /></p>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe maximum number of edges in an undirected graph (simple) with 52 vertices and 3 components are __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1225,1225],"answerText":"1225","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t1225</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e35a7f729b179330efe0.png\" /></p>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a random sample of size n from an exponential distribution with parameter <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc9e24999cb809d5bf4a.png\" /> The sample mean is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c7aac04854c84260c1a.png\" /> Evaluate the following statements:</p>\n<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e358e44825a85ee20e4.png\" /> is an unbiased estimator of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c576048b4d43d13c504.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/dabd8fc14b6cea59d19e.png\" /> is a maximum likelihood estimator of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/bf/bf6be6da0f51272bddb0.png\" /> is a maximum likelihood estimator of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/012b4ca7f8e6e61cd429.png\" /><br />\n\tWhich of the above statements is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/118492d7a80f3e62ef04.png\" /></p>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tMatch the items in <strong>Column-I</strong> with the appropriate descriptions in <strong>Column-II:</strong></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/94156e0f1a6369edb3ec.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&bull; Rejection Sampling &rarr; Generates samples and filters them<br />\n\t&bull; Iterative Deepening Search (IDS*) &rarr; Combines depth and breadth search<br />\n\t&bull; Heuristic Function &rarr; Uses heuristic for cost estimation</p>"},{"n":19,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a relation <em>R</em> (<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>, <em>D</em>, <em>E</em>) with the following functional dependencies:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/028228622e316839699c.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThe total number of super keys present in the relation are _______.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[28,28],"answerText":"28","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t28</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74dd0a604190569b8fe9.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec7964e5fd05a41c0848.png\" /></p>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"To evaluate any expression whose operands are integer values, a single stack is enough."},{"key":"B","html":"Conversion of Infix to Postfix requires 1 stack."},{"key":"C","html":"Both (a) and (b)"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Since, the expression content is simple, that is only numeric values, hence it can be evaluated tack.<br />\n\t&bull; An infix operation can be converted to a postfix operation using single stack.</p>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tA fair dice is rolled, Let A denoted the event of obtaining a number less than or equal to 5 and 13 denote the event of obtaining and odd number. Then which of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b44aaee9d4975fc55670.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/44499ff3c02d76127e0f.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fb16e6332a8532991b1f.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d643baf7aea67469266e.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9ca956d63d76ff5459d5.png\" /></p>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following functions:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b25572f58423990b8871.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the following is true at <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/185a686a027a4d10c051.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Neither continuous nor differentiable"},{"key":"B","html":"Continuous but not differentiable"},{"key":"C","html":"Continuous and differentiable"},{"key":"D","html":"Differential but not continuous"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a07e74895c6e44b6c585.png\" /></p>"},{"n":23,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhat is the standard deviation of a uniformly distributed variable between 0 and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a9/a93e985190ca0e8dffe4.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/7694cef20139aecf52b0.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0004397327f6228fa1a.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d7ae1fd4c6cc93ea58c6.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/005e4611d8f142941681.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/441d122b0cbc17cd0549.png\" /></p>"},{"n":24,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) can be used only for unsupervised learning tasks.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Decision Trees provide a clear and interpretable structure for decision-making processes.<br />\n\tWhich of the above is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) are mainly used for supervised learning tasks not unsupervised ones. They can be adapted for unsupervised tasks in some cases but this is not their most common use. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Decision Tree provide a clear and interpretable structure for decision-making processes, making it easy to understand how decision are made. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following well formed formulae:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ba/ba6e0600a925180233a0.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"I and III are equivalent"},{"key":"B","html":"III and IV are equivalent"},{"key":"C","html":"I and II are equivalent"},{"key":"D","html":"II and IV are equivalent"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/84/84c1742fb0cce6311cf3.png\" /></p>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following Python code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/964f298ad98a5c041fe3.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Two string are equal"},{"key":"B","html":"Two string are unequal"},{"key":"C","html":"Run time error"},{"key":"D","html":"Compile time error"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)<br />\n\tIn the given code !== not used to check inequality between the two string.</p>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tFor relation <em>R</em>(<em>P</em>, <em>Q</em>, <em>R</em>, <em>S</em>, <em>T</em>, <em>U</em>) with the FD set <em>F</em> = {<em>P</em> → <em>S</em>, <em>S</em> → <em>T</em>, <em>R</em> → <em>U</em>}. What is the minimum relation required for storing R such that highest normal form satisfied in 3NF ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4,4],"answerText":"4","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t4</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85b14ea889f02cc53a90.png\" /></p>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tA man has 5 Apples, 3 Oranges and 3 Graphs. If the Man eats one piece of fruit each day, and only the type of fruit matters, in how many different ways can these fruits be consumed?</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9240,9240],"answerText":"9240","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t9240</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c82cf9f0bd46dc3ce6c.png\" /></p>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following Python code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ffb920e6a3f3dd1b28bf.png\" /></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[302000,302000],"answerText":"302000","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t302000</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ee/ee87757e3ba58c0a2030.png\" /></p>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Roll-up operation in OLAP summarizes data by moving up a hierarchy, leading to higherlevel aggregates.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Drill-down in OLAP increases data detail by navigating down a hierarchy, revealing finer granularity.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; The roll-up operation in OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) aggregates data by moving up the hierarchy levels (e.g., from individual sales to regional totals). So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; The drill-down operation in OLAP allows users to view more detailed data by moving down the hierarchy (e.g., from regional totals to individual sales). So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":31,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tMatch the items in <strong>Column-1</strong> with the items in <strong>Column-2</strong> in the following table:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/179c94b7562f6cf07602.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Independent Component Analysis &rarr; Dimensionality Reduction<br />\n\t&bull; Naive Bayes Classifier &rarr; Generative Model<br />\n\t&bull; Multilayer Perceptron (MLP) &rarr; Discriminative Model</p>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the formula is correct for given sentence:<br />\n\t“No students are allowed to carry smartphone”</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d2a935b9f67a17edb08b.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26d0c17553d3f85b5672.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/547ed73e2e7ec5fe662f.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f353b532a697178445eb.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b740e02b8be24a56f3f.png\" /></p>"},{"n":33,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/67d2249dbb6803aa05b1.png\" /> is a characteristic of 3 × 3 diagonal matrix, then trace of matrix m is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,5],"answerText":"5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t5</p>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe values of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b6e6e0415e6a543fdd66.png\" /> for which the function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/9435bd28010e8d398914.png\" /> is NOT continuous are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4"},{"key":"B","html":"-4"},{"key":"C","html":"-1"},{"key":"D","html":"1"}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/df4b266e2a2905550be0.png\" /></p>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tYou have a dataset of 90 samples with two classes, Class A and Class B. At a particular node, the entropy before the split is 0.98. After splitting on a feature, the dataset is divided into two nodes with the following distribution: Node 1 has 40 samples (30 in Class A, 10 in Class B) with an entropy of 0.81, and Node 2 has 50 samples (20 in Class A, 30 in Class B) with an entropy of 0.92. What is the Information Gain from this split? [Upto 2 decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.11,0.11],"answerText":"0.11","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.11</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b9b22a017bf361aff851.png\" /></p>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tLet <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22df27711a6fdf367563.png\" /> is ________.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Ω(n)"},{"key":"B","html":"Ο(n)"},{"key":"C","html":"θ(n)"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/786032f81fafcf9756b0.png\" /></p>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>X</em> is a random variable with normal distribution having a mean of 25 and standard deviation of 4, then probability of (20 ≤ <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/188d110b620771d922f4.png\" /> ≤ 30) is ________. [Upto 3 decimal places]<br />\n\t[Take P(0 ≤ Z ≤ 1.25) = 0.3944]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.7888,0.7888],"answerText":"0.7888","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.7888</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/0441913b71a6dad8bbe2.png\" /></p>"},{"n":38,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Regularization in Ridge Regression involves adding a penalty proportional to the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients."},{"key":"B","html":"Principal Component Analysis (PCA) reduces dimensionality by transforming features into a new set of orthogonal components."},{"key":"C","html":"Random Forests use a single decision tree to make predictions."},{"key":"D","html":"Gradient Descent is used to optimize the parameters in a neural network."}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, d)<br />\n\t&bull; Ridge Regression uses <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> regularization, which adds a penalty proportional to the sum of the square of coefficients, not their absolute value. So, option (a) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; PCA reduces dimensionality by transforming the original features into orthogonal component that capture the most variance in the data. So, option (b) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Random Forests is an ensemble method that combines predictions from multiple decision tree. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Gradient Descent is used to optimize the parameters of a neural network by iteratively adjusting weight to minimize the loss function. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":39,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhat is the maximum number of nodes in B<sup>+</sup> tree possible with order 4 and number of levels 5 ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[341,341],"answerText":"341","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t341</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e4b9be0070448f841c29.png\" /></p>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a hash table of size 11. Let h(k) = k mode 11 be the has function used. A sequence of records with keys {33, 68, 62, 47, 48, 60, 104, 23, 19, 120, 87} is inserted into an initially empty hash table, the bins of which are indexed from zero to ten.<br />\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"If, collisions are resolved by linear probing then maximum number of comparisons in worst case can be 2."},{"key":"B","html":"If chaining is used to resolve collision, the average chain length will be 1.09."},{"key":"C","html":"Both of these"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8288a83622be000fb9f.png\" /></p>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf matrix <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06e71ee8c66c79ad194d.png\" /> then the rank of matrix <em>A</em> is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t2</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0b/0be5776a89c2011db239.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a7/a77522b05ecc439a9257.png\" /></p>"},{"n":42,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following function(s) is/are a bijection from <em>R</em> to <em>R</em>?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/71ded7c12ffd7e9f4c07.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/48417fd3bae79ace9810.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/87/8765e9066ae8db9d10de.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26542aeb25dde104e2ec.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c229670a04d8deb5c9e.png\" /></p>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tA dataset with <em>N</em> samples is classified into <em>K</em> classes using a Naive Bayes classifier. Each sample is described using <em>D</em> categorical features, where each feature can take <em>V<sub>j</sub></em> values, where <em>j</em> = 1, 2, ..., <em>D</em>. How many parameters need to be estimated?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/df26ab68c92fb1230daa.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7fe11927bed02ccc1e3f.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8fee0760d64cbcd8c12a.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b21c69202398c69e83e4.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3c84c56de485cc7f8abe.png\" /></p>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : In IDA*, the search is repeated with increasing depth limits until the solution is found.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : A* search is uses a Priority queue for node expansion.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tNeither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Iterative Deepening A* (IDA*) performs a series of depth-first searches with increasing depth limits based on the f-cost until it finds the solution. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; A* search algorithm uses a priority queue (often implemented as a min-heap) to keep track of nodes to be expanded based on their f-cost values. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d312dbb5dce2cd651dcd.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tAssume Node is structure type with two member ‘value’ and ‘next’. Identify the node value printed by the above code. If non-empty linked list header is passed to the function find?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Last element of list"},{"key":"B","html":"Second element of list"},{"key":"C","html":"First element of list"},{"key":"D","html":"Middle element of list"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)<br />\n\tP1 traverse the list one node at time.<br />\n\tP2 skips one node each time. If moves when P2 reaches NULL, P1 will indeed be pointing to the middle node of the linked list.</p>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider Vamshi decides to toss a fair coin repeatedly until he gets a tail. He makes atmost 4 tosses. The value of variance (T) is ________</p>\n<p>\n\t(variable T denotes the number of tosses).</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f28d0ec6540543827736.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bcd867a4fde1d146a809.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/caa54a7d9a445a454d99.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d247495e179e65b2484d.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/912a9f143766ca9aaa2a.png\" /></p>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tLet the minimum, maximum, mean, and standard deviation values for the attribute salary of software engineers be 50000, 120000, 80000 and 15000, respectively. The Z-score normalized salary value of $95,000 is closest to which ONE of the following options?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.87"},{"key":"B","html":"1.00"},{"key":"C","html":"1.33"},{"key":"D","html":"1.67"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1a/1a5655ef68ea1f51daae.png\" /></p>"},{"n":48,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe probability density function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c98e4288eab50cd53bd9.png\" /> of a variable continuous random variable <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d61d754627aa2bfe444.png\" /> is defined by</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a1d9b159ddb2db757121.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThen the approx value of P is ________. [Upto 2 decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[66.66,66.67],"answerText":"66.66 [66.66 - 66.67]","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t66.66 [66.66 - 66.67]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a594780adb9fc19c74c6.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a7/a738f5508ceca95fa042.png\" /></p>"},{"n":49,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are true?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : In Ridge Regression, regularization is applied to prevent overfitting by penalizing large coefficients.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : The k-NN algorithm performs well with high-dimensional data due to the curse of dimensionality.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&bull; Ridge Regression includes a regularization the <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> norm of the coefficients to be penalize large coefficients, which helps to prevent overfitting. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is true.<br />\n\t&bull; The k-NN algorithm does not performs well with high-dimensional data because the curse of dimensionality makes distance between points less meaningful leading to poor performance. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is false.</p>"},{"n":50,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following is tautology?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/04d23286965b4a65d33e.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/7442b0cd771461c71c3a.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/631d007a2298c59ebc31.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"Both (b) and (c)"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/564d225438b2ff7e32f4.png\" /></p>"},{"n":51,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tAssume <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are matrix of size n × n, which of the following is false?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>A</em> is invertiable, then <em>ABA</em><sup>–1</sup> = <em>B</em>.</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>A</em> is an indempotent non-singular matrix, then <em>A</em> must be the identify matrix.</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tIf the coefficient matrix <em>A</em> of the system <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80c386a307178b7baa94.png\" /> is invertible, then the system has infinitely many solution.</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>AB</em> = <em>B</em> then <em>B</em> is identity matrix.</p>"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, c, d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8aa12264e9d4399f3209.png\" /></p>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe maximum value of the function:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a9/a9773bd74a87ca387627.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tIn interval of [–3 to 3] is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[25,25],"answerText":"25","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t25</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/0477a7594fb23b3e9b70.png\" /></p>"},{"n":53,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following program code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/8891b90ee897f647a754.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the following represents the running time for run (n) function?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Ο(log n)"},{"key":"B","html":"Ο(log (log (n))"},{"key":"C","html":"Ο(log ∗ (n))"},{"key":"D","html":"Ο(n)"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff9f6eae53d714257c6a.png\" /></p>"},{"n":54,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following relational schema:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9f6052edb5c294d21275.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the following query represent find the Pid of parts supplied by at least two different suppliers.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85749d1009f391e46128.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0a/0a780f3af3749ac64c75.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/342e8f1842a46a6b1662.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d9aab1e3af55693752a.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, d)</p>"},{"n":55,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Naive Bayes classifier assumes that features are dependent on each other given the class label."},{"key":"B","html":"Hierarchical clustering methods include single-linkage and complete-linkage approaches."},{"key":"C","html":"Naive Bayes classifier is used for dimensionality reduction."},{"key":"D","html":"Hierarchical clustering requires the number of clusters to be specified before analysis."}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Naive Bayes assumes features are independent given the class label. So, option (a) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Hierarchical clustering include methods like single-linkage (minimum distance) and completelinkage (maximum distance) approaches. So, option (b) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Naive Bayes is for classifier, not dimensionality reduction, PCA is responsible for dimensionality reduction. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Hierarchical clustering does not require specifying the number of cluster before hand. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":56,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tMin heap tree can be constructed in 2 ways for a given sequence of elements:<br />\n\t<strong>Method 1:</strong> Insert element one after the other.<br />\n\t<strong>Method 2:</strong> Insert all the elements in one go and then perform all the heapify operations.<br />\n\tBased on these two methods for creating min heap, select the correct options from the following:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Both the methods will create exactly same min heap tree for all possible input sequence of elements."},{"key":"B","html":"Both the methods may create different min heap tree for some input sequence of elements."},{"key":"C","html":"Method 1 will take Ο(n logn) time to create the min heap tree."},{"key":"D","html":"Method 2 will take Ο(n) time to create the min heap tree."}],"answer":["B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, c, d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8271eeecddb12f48099.png\" /></p>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : In a connected undirected graph <em>G</em> = (<em>V</em>, <em>E</em>) with distinct edge costs, the cheapest edge belongs to every minimum spanning tree.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : In a connected undirected graph <em>G</em> = (<em>V</em>, <em>E</em>) with distinct edge costs, the most expensive edge is excluded from every minimum spanning tree.<br />\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tNeither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d7b55e3164fa46722e02.png\" /></p>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a matrix [<em>p</em>] = <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7c/7c8fb47cd0fa9a6d1ae2.png\" /> If two eigen value are 1, 3, then number of values that a can take is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"2"},{"key":"D","html":"3"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d1da9f1e48b8be10236e.png\" /></p>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tFind the value of K so that function f defined below is continuous at <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b1641dc5f27debff99b2.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/532e688e936ee05174cb.png\" /></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1,1],"answerText":"1","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t1</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/de61ba390623044e54ad.png\" /></p>"},{"n":60,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tSelect the correct statement from the following:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The largest element in the min heap tree will always occupy a leaf node."},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tThe worst case height in a binary search tree can be Ο(<em>n</em>).</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tThe worst case height in an AVL tree is Ο(log <em>n</em>).</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tGiven <em>n</em> elements, a min heap can be created in Ο(n) time.</p>"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b, c, d)<br />\n\t(a) Since the largest element should remain in bottom of the tree, any element less than it will trigger a heapify operation. So the largest element will definitely come to leaf node level.</p>"},{"n":61,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a B<sup>+</sup> tree in which search key is 15 bytes long, block size is 2048 bytes, record pointer is 12 bytes long and block pointer is 10 bytes long. The maximum number of keys that can be accommodated in each leaf node of the tree is ________. (Assume order of leaf node refers to number of keys present in the node)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[75,75],"answerText":"75","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t75</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6bd6092cd2d8bfce56a9.png\" /></p>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements about SVM Kernels is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tThe polynomial Kernel function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c113edf32ec84ab9cf75.png\" /> allows the model to learn polynomial decision boundaries.</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tThe radial basis function (RBF) Kernel is defined as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a6/a6404e698219d6f46fa0.png\" /> is a parameter that controls the width of the Gaussian function.</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tThe linear Kernel function is equivalent to the dot product of the input features, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c5/c517f2c4edefc4708c89.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"The choice of Kernel function does not affect the complexity of the resulting SVM model."}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b, c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d44552fd5e19a0d1b83b.png\" /></p>"},{"n":63,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tLet <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/eae8ae0b7650573b1093.png\" /> is the 3 × 3 identify matrix, which of the following statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tEigen value of <em>A</em> are 1, 2, –2.</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tEigen value of <em>B</em> are 1, 1, 1.</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tDeterminant of <em>B</em> is 1.</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tDeterminant of <em>B</em> cannot be determined.</p>"}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, c)</p>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tSuppose <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> are random variables such that</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/61/6107ad13806c4571387d.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tBy using above values the following expression are evaluated.<br />\n\t(i) <em>E</em>(<em>X</em> + 2<em>Y</em>) = <em>P</em><br />\n\t(ii) <em>E</em>(<em>XY</em>) = <em>q</em><br />\n\t(iii) Var(<em>X</em> – 2<em>Y</em> + 1) = r<br />\n\tThe value of <em>pq</em> + <em>r</em> is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[20,20],"answerText":"20","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t20</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83b59e471d88162f5b70.png\" /></p>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tThe worst case time complexity for the following C program is:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/86846e874979c0a154c2.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tΟ(2<em><sup>n</sup></em>)</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tΟ(3<em><sup>n</sup></em>)</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tΟ(<em>n</em><sup>3</sup>)</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tΟ(<em>n</em><sup>2</sup>)</p>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/397e663c8a0ae27362f1.png\" /></p>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"NAT":20,"MSQ":10},"withoutKey":0}};
